": "73047ed890e69c9e97755acf6a351174cc85b2ef", "length": "4924.59", "height": "480", "width": "640"}, {"name": "The_Phantom_Planet.mpeg", "source": "original", "format": "MPEG2", "title": "The Phantom Planet", "md5": "271c718afae7e54b294f7a4bd4083acc", "mtime": "1205499374", "size": "1969657863", "crc32": "a5cad748", "sha1": "9719162fbc0eebe9b7527d8b8a84017002306795", "length": "4924.55", "height": "480", "width": "640"}, {"name": "The_Phantom_Planet.ogv", "source": "derivative", "format": "Ogg Video", "original": "The_Phantom_Planet.mpeg", "md5": "6a7d4dabe89ef5dc191d9b675353eb49", "mtime": "1227922019", "size": "349439064", "crc32": "f26fc793", "sha1": "5068efce1d376edae1d8f032841ee827c7e61417", "length": "4924.55", "height": "304", "width": "400"}, {"name": "The_Phantom_Planet.png", "source": "derivative", "format": "PNG", "original": "The_Phantom_Planet.mp3", "mtime": "1540595743", "size": "11869", "md5": "aca160c0e3cea4021b3e7d14cb8dbfd1", "crc32": "fe7dd0a1", "sha1": "612d5e8744dac2527483dfade5899f79a3977297"}, {"name": "The_Phantom_Planet_512kb.mp4", "source": "derivative", "format": "512Kb MPEG4", "original": "The_Phantom_Planet.mpeg", "md5": "2c2fec90e9bf9c0299a6acfad2499538", "mtime": "1227919017", "size": "358027527", "crc32": "34702351", "sha1": "5a36b04e430fcc23444cfbde368a5cbc5a54ac58", "length": "4924.55", "height": "240", "width": "320"}, {"name": "__ia_thumb.jpg", "source": "original", "mtime": "1654297068", "size": "1869", "md5": "015a8342c929bfbbe98f7a12351bdb0d", "crc32": "6899b1de", "sha1": "14a335c089db54b0c40b31004cb080eafbd59fcb", "format": "Item Tile", "rotation": "0"}], "files_count": 97, "item_last_updated": 1762318696, "item_size": 3250308305, "metadata": {"identifier": "Phantom_Planet", "title": "The Phantom Planet", "creator": "Fred Gebhardt", "mediatype": "movies", "collection": ["film_scifi", "feature_films", "moviesandfilms"], "description": "A spaceship is drawn towards a planet populated by tiny people where the atmosphere shrinks the astronauts as well.\n\nThis film was featured on the television program Mystery Science Theater 3000.\n\nYou can find an MP4 of this film <a href=\"http://www.archive.org/details/PhantomPlanet\" rel=\"ugc nofollow\">here</a>.\n\nYou can find out more about this film on its <a href=\"http://imdb.com/title/tt0055294/\" rel=\"ugc nofollow\">IMDB page</a>.", "date": "1961", "year": "1961", "subject": "sci-fi; MST3K; space travel", "licenseurl": "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/publicdomain/", "publicdate": "2008-03-14 18:01:06", "addeddate": "2008-03-14 18:00:16", "uploader": "dondeeley@gmail.com", "updater": ["drworm01", "twainbough", "jordonz"], "updatedate": ["2008-03-14 18:05:52", "2008-03-15 15:19:13", "2008-05-15 17:29:24"], "director": "William Marshall", "publisher": "Four Crown Productions Inc.", "sound": "sound", "color": "b&w", "runtime": "1:22:04", "language": "English", "backup_location": "ia903601_27", "closed_captioning": "no", "collection_added": ["feature_films", "moviesandfilms"]}, "reviews": [{"reviewbody": "Wow!! This was great. I sat through the whole thing, knowing exactly where MST3K would be punctuating it. \nFor me, it's the overly phallic spaceship, which I'm sure started life as a vibrator. No longer working, the producer's wife still couldn't bare to part with \"Ol Faithful\", so she told her cuckhold hubby to put it in his next film somewhere...\nAnd that was just the beginning of this plotless affair... \n\nEverything is classic, from using a chunk of lava rock, and calling it a planet, to the spiky broken-glass looking things controlling the gravity thingy, the bits of linoleum representing dissintigrating plates, it's all so-much camp, and had me laughing through-out this whole cinematic suppository. \nSimply for entertainment value, I give it a full (5) *****;; \nFor the ham and cheezy acting (5)*****. In fact, for the space walk alone, where there is not even the pretense that there's no gravity--boy that 1 stabilizing fin is conveniently placed so we can stroll across it. \nNice classic lines: \"push that radar harder, keep pushing it harder\"\nOverall, a (5)*****, and a must-see.", "reviewtitle": "This is only the beginning....", "reviewer": "daves_not_here", "reviewdate": "2009-01-12 15:48:26", "createdate": "2009-01-12 15:48:26", "stars": "5"}, {"reviewbody": "I agree with everything Dave (who isn't here) is saying, but this was one of the most unremarkable and unmemorable movies I have ever seen.\n\nI got this in a boxed set of cheesy sci fi movies (yes, I search them out), and have seen it several times.  Each time is new to me because so few scenes stand out.\n\nI give it a 5 for cheese value, but the feeling of having wasted an hour and a few minutes drops the rating to a 3.", "reviewtitle": "Unremarkable, but worth watching", "reviewer": "salt4pepper", "reviewdate": "2009-06-11 17:46:15", "createdate": "2009-06-11 17:46:15", "stars": "3"}, {"reviewbody": "With its good production values, good cast and even a worthy background score, this is solid '50s science fiction - that is until minute 28 when it makes a sudden left turn into downtown Schlockville, with our hero landing on a mini-planet full of 6 inch people, the cute ones in miniskirts. Rather than a disappointment, it turns this flick into a whole different kind of fun, featuring silent film star Francis X Bushman, beautiful girls including Coleen Gray and one of the funniest monsters ever. The planet-side plot involves a trial with an all-miniskirt jury, a push-pole duel to the death (almost), a space war against the dreaded \"Solarites\" and the aforementioned monster stumbling around papier-mache cave sets carrying an unconscious cutie. What more could you want? Don't miss this one! CAST NOTES: In spite of her good looks and acting talent (see \"Nightmare Alley\" costarring Tyrone Power) Coleen Gray's film career never managed to go very far. If the old studio system had survived, it might have been a different story. Francis X Bushman's acting career spanned from 1909 to 1966, during which he appeared in no less than 209 productions, usually in starring roles.", "reviewtitle": "Think Small", "reviewer": "picfixer", "reviewdate": "2010-01-31 22:26:44", "createdate": "2010-01-31 22:26:44", "stars": "4"}, {"reviewbody": "nice", "reviewtitle": "must watch !", "reviewer": "nigeldavahah", "reviewdate": "2010-11-03 20:49:31", "createdate": "2010-11-03 20:49:31", "stars": "5"}, {"reviewbody": "This film is a klassic of its kind-- great fun in a silly, campy kind of way. Dolores Faith was luscious in this movie. I found myself getting wistful at the movie's end, wishing for a happy ending for Chapman and Zetha. Thank you for posting and sharing this movie.", "reviewtitle": "Great fun", "reviewer": "hawtdawg", "reviewdate": "2011-03-20 16:07:09", "createdate": "2011-03-20 16:07:09", "stars": "5"}, {"reviewbody": "It is wonderful to know that modesty prevails when one shrinks down on an alien world that one's undergarments shrink as well!\nImagine the embarassment if you shrank and your \"Fruit of the Looms\" no longer covered your private parts!!!!!  \nThis is good campy fun.", "reviewtitle": "Thank you, to the gods in charge of shrinking!!!!!", "reviewer": "I_h8_screen_names", "reviewdate": "2013-11-08 01:42:39", "createdate": "2013-11-08 01:42:39", "stars": "5"}, {"reviewbody": "Great move for when it was made. A must see for all Science Fiction fans.", "reviewtitle": "Great 5 stars", "reviewer": "ezz913", "reviewer_itemname": "@ezz913", "reviewdate": "2018-01-02 23:53:57", "createdate": "2018-01-02 23:53:57", "stars": "5"}, {"reviewtitle": "Spacesuits", "reviewbody": "The spacesuits worn by the pilots at the analog controls of their ship look like leftover lizard men costumes ", "stars": "0", "reviewer": "qwerty1235", "reviewdate": "2020-12-09 09:06:37", "createdate": "2020-12-09 09:04:21", "reviewer_itemname": "@qwerty1235"}, {"reviewtitle": "Not supposed to be STAR WARS STUPID!!!", "reviewbody": "In 1961 we were thrilled to have such great movies, so go stuff a sock in it.", "stars": "5", "reviewer": "Roadmuffin", "reviewdate": "2022-06-03 23:08:36", "createdate": "2022-06-03 22:57:42", "reviewer_itemname": "@roadmuffin"}], "server": "dn800307.us.archive.org", "simplelists": {"solo_manifest": {"solo_manifest_dn800307": {"sys_changed_by": {"source": "task", "task_id": "5413555532"}, "sys_last_changed": "2026-06-03 08:39:36.597503"}}}, "solo": true, "uniq": 1045440580, "workable_servers": ["dn800307.us.archive.org"]}